-so that no reported difference rests on having given the alternative too little
-room. These are results about a model whose functional forms are stipulated rather
-than measured. They establish that each prediction is well posed, that the
-signature it names is measurable, and that the framework generates that signature
-where a natural comparator does not; they are not evidence about the behaviour of
-biological or artificial cognitive systems, and they do not stand in for the
-empirical tests described in Section~\ref{sec:limitations}.
-
-A companion study takes up a narrower empirical
